# illog UI rules

This project has a custom design system at `@illog/ui` backed by tokens in `@illog/themes`. Always reuse the existing primitives. The full reference is in `services/web/public/llms-full.txt` — load it whenever you need component or token details.

## Hard rules

1. **No raw color, spacing, radius, font, blur, depth, or stroke values** in component code. Reference `@illog/themes` tokens via `@illog/ui` sprinkles or recipes.
2. **New UI primitives go in `packages/ui/src/components/<Name>/`**, never inside `services/app`. App code only composes existing `@illog/ui` primitives.
3. **No deep imports**. Always `import { X } from '@illog/ui'`. Never `@illog/ui/src/...`.
4. **Vanilla Extract only** for styling — `@vanilla-extract/sprinkles`, `@vanilla-extract/recipes`, `@vanilla-extract/css`, `@vanilla-extract/dynamic`. No Tailwind, no CSS modules, no styled-components.
5. **Boolean props use `is` / `has` prefixes** (`isDisabled`, `hasError`). Variants are string union literals, never enums.
6. **React 19 ref-as-prop** — accept `ref?: Ref<HTMLXxxElement>` directly in props. Do not use `forwardRef`.
7. **Compound components** expose a `use<Name>Context` hook (see `Selector` for the canonical pattern).

## Component creation checklist

Before adding a new component to `packages/ui`:

- [ ] Confirm no existing primitive covers the use case (check `packages/ui/src/index.ts` and `llms-full.txt`).
- [ ] Folder layout: `index.ts`, `<Name>.tsx`, `<name>.css.ts`, `types.ts` (optional), `<Name>.test.tsx`.
- [ ] Export from `packages/ui/src/index.ts` (the only public surface).
- [ ] Style with sprinkles for tokenized values, recipes for variant-driven styling.
- [ ] Add a story in `services/storybook/stories/UI/<Name>/`.
- [ ] Run `pnpm --filter @illog/ui typecheck` and `test`.
- [ ] If you added a token: regenerate via `pnpm --filter @illog/themes build:css` and `pnpm --filter @illog/ui build:color`.
- [ ] Regenerate AI context: `pnpm gen:ai-context`.

## Auto-generated files — do not hand-edit

- `packages/ui/src/core/tokens/generatedColors.ts`
- `packages/ui/src/assets/icons/*`
- `packages/ui/components.spec.json`
- `services/web/public/llms-full.txt`

## Discovery order when looking for a component

1. `packages/ui/src/index.ts` exports — if it exists, use it.
2. `services/web/public/llms-full.txt` for the full prop spec.
3. `services/storybook/stories/UI/<Component>/` for usage examples.
4. Only if no existing primitive fits: propose adding one to `packages/ui`.
